/-!
# `Work.FeitSibley.Coherence.engine`

The *engine* of the Feit–Sibley coherence theorem (Peterfalvi II, Appendice XII, Théorème
p. 289): the `τ`-coherence machinery (`linearShift`, `coherent_of_linearShift`,
`coherent_of_card_le_one`, `coherent_of_feit_step`), Milestone A (`𝒮(Q')` is coherent), the
size bound `two_mul_card_D_add_one_le_card_of_ne` and the `H`-invariance of the lower central
series of `S`.

This module is the part of the proof of `Work.FeitSibley.Coherence.coherent_scriptS` that the
*pure* reduction lemmas (`Coherence/step2`, `Coherence/step1`, `Coherence/reduction`) need;
the final theorem lives in `Coherence/coherent_scriptS.lean`, which imports this file (thereby
avoiding an import cycle).

This file contains the general *linear-shift* extension engine: a shift of `τ` by a multiple
`χ(1) • a` of a single vector `a` agrees with `τ` on `ℤ[𝒮]⁰` automatically, and the Gram-matrix
condition for the shifted family is exactly what is needed for `Coherent`.

## Reduction to a single vector `a` (proved: `coherent_of_linearShift`)

Every `ℤ`-linear extension `τ'` of `τ|ℤ[𝒮]⁰` to `ℤ[𝒮]` has the form `τ' χ = τ χ + χ(1) • a` for a
single vector `a` (the quotient `ℤ[𝒮]/ℤ[𝒮]⁰ ≅ ℤ` is generated by the degree).  Hence the theorem
is equivalent to the existence of `a : G → ℂ` with

* `∀ χ ∈ 𝒮, IsVChar (indLin χ + χ(1) • a)` (automatic if `a ∈ ℤ[Irr G]`, since every degree in
  `𝒮` is a multiple of `d = |D|`), and
* the Gram condition `⟨τ χ + χ(1)•a, τ ψ + ψ(1)•a⟩ = ⟨χ,ψ⟩` on `𝒮`.

## Roadmap of the Peterfalvi argument (App. XII, pp. 288–295)

`Y := 𝒮(Q')` (`Q' = [Q,Q]`) consists of characters of degree `d = |D|` (all of
`𝒮(R)`, `R ≥ Q'`, do), so `Y` is coherent by FT Lemma 10.1 (`Coherence.coherent_of_norm_two_lift`).
`X := 𝒮 - 𝒮(Z)` (`Z = [Q1,Q1] ∩ Z(Q1)`) is coherent by the chief-series/Isaacs-7.14 induction
(steps (1)–(3) of the source).  The two-block argument (steps (4)–(8)) then produces the
`e_i ∈ ±Irr G` for `X` and `e'_j ∈ ±Irr G` for `Y` whose mutual orthogonality and the
congruence `ψ(z) ≡ ψ(1) mod |Q|` give the extension.  The pieces already formalised in this
workspace are listed in the session handoff.

## Status of this file (see the session handoff for the full account)

**Proved here** (all sorry-free):

* the linear-shift engine `linearShift`, `linearShift_apply_mem`, `coherent_of_linearShift`;
* `coherent_of_card_le_one` — a set of at most one irreducible of non-zero degree is coherent for
  *any* `τ`.  (This is what replaces Peterfalvi's assertion `|𝒮(Q')| ≥ 2` in milestone A: no
  independent lower bound on `|𝒮(Q')|` is needed.)
* `coherent_of_feit_step` — the "Feit step": to show `Coherent S τ` it suffices to rule out, for
  every `χ ∈ S ∖ S₀`, the situation in which Feit's criterion `coherent_union_singleton`
  (Isaacs 7.14, Peterfalvi Lemma 1a) produces a *strict* inequality.  Its engine is
  `exists_chi_not_coherent`, the contrapositive of 7.14 (delegated, now proved, in
  `Coherence/exists_chi_not_coherent.lean`).
* **Milestone A** (Peterfalvi's `𝒮(Q')` is coherent): `coherent_scriptSR_Qcomm`, together with
  `scriptSR_Qcomm_deg`, `scriptSR_Qcomm_orthonormal`, `scriptSR_Qcomm_isometryOn`.
* `two_mul_card_D_add_one_le_card_of_ne` — `2|D| < |A|` for a `D`-invariant `A ≤ Q₁` with
  `|A| ≠ |D| + 1`, the size bound used in the arithmetic of steps (1)–(3).
* `H_le_normalizer_lowerCentralSeries` — the terms of the lower central series of `S` are
  normalised by `H`: these are Peterfalvi's subgroups `S₁ ⊴ H`, `S₁ ⊆ S'`.

**Peterfalvi's step (2) is DONE**, in the companion module
`Submission.Work.FeitSibley.Coherence.step2` (namespace `Work.FeitSibley.Coherence`):

* `numeric_contradiction` — the arithmetic of the step;
* `indLin_apply_one`, `isVChar_indLin_zSpan_scriptS`, `isVChar_indLin_zSpan0_scriptS` — the
  `IsVChar`/degree-zero conditions needed by `coherent_of_feit_step` in the Feit–Sibley setting;
* `commutator_lt_self_of_ne_bot` — `⁅S,S⁆ < S` for a nontrivial nilpotent `S`;
* `coherent_scriptS_of_coherent_scriptSR` — **the reduction**

  `(∃ θ ∈ Irr Q₁, θ linear, θ ≠ 1) → Coherent (𝒮(S')) → Coherent 𝒮`,

  obtained by walking up the lower central series `γ i = S.lowerCentralSeries i` from `γ 1 = S'`
  to `γ m = ⊥`, one application of `coherent_of_feit_step` per step.  Everything else has been
  discharged: `deg_sq_le_of_mem_scriptSR_center` (the degree bound, with the *full* centre
  `Z(Q₁) = h.centerQ1`), `scriptSR_Qcomm_nonempty`, and the numerical input
  `two_mul_card_D_sq_le_card_Q1_sub_two_mul_card_centerQ1`
  (`2|D|² ≤ (|Q₁|-2)·|Z(Q₁)|`, from `two_mul_card_D_add_one_le_card_Q1` and
  `D_dvd_card_sub_one`).  For `D ≠ ⊥` the remaining hypothesis `hlin` is also discharged —
  `Q1_isNilpotent_of_D_ne_bot` is Thompson's theorem (via
  `Work.ThompsonFrobenius.isNilpotent_of_fpf_pow` + `GlaubermanZJProp`) giving
  `exists_nontrivial_linear_of_D_ne_bot` — so that
  `coherent_scriptS_of_coherent_scriptSR_of_D_ne_bot` reduces the whole theorem, for `D ≠ ⊥`,
  to `Coherent (𝒮(S'))` alone.

**The exact Gram matrix of `Ind_H^G` on `𝒮`** (proved this session, in
`Coherence/cfInner_indLin_scriptS.lean`):

  `⟨Ind χ, Ind ψ⟩ = δ_{χψ} + (( |G:H| - 1 ) / |H|)·χ(1)·ψ(1)`  for `χ, ψ ∈ 𝒮`,

i.e. the rank-one perturbation `I + γ·ddᵀ` (`d_χ = χ(1)`) of the identity.  Consequently, in
`Coherence/reduction.lean`, **the whole theorem is reduced to a single explicit vector**:

  `coherent_scriptS_of_exists_a` — if `a : G → ℂ` and `f : ℂ` satisfy `⟨Ind χ, a⟩ = f·χ(1)` for
  all `χ ∈ 𝒮`, `⟨a,a⟩ = -(|G:H|-1)/|H| - 2·Re f`, and `Ind χ + χ(1) • a` is a virtual character of
  `G` for all `χ ∈ 𝒮`, then `𝒮` is coherent.  Peterfalvi's `e_i`, `e'_j` are the irreducible
  constituents of the `Ind χ + χ(1) • a`, and the congruence of his step (7) is what forces `a`
  to be integral.

**Remaining work: Peterfalvi's steps (1), (3) and (4)–(8)**, i.e. the construction of `a` / the
proof that `𝒮(S')` is coherent.  Step (1) handles `|Q₁|` divisible by two primes, step (3) the
case `Q₁` a nonabelian `p`-group (`p` odd), steps (4)–(8) the two-block argument; with the Gram
matrix above, step (5) is automatic and step (6) is a one-line computation.

The arithmetic of steps (1)–(3) needs the two numerical inputs

  `2·|D| + 1 ≤ |Q₁|`  and  `(|Q₁| - 2)·|Z| ≥ 2·|D|²`  (`Z = [Q₁,Q₁] ∩ Z(Q₁)`),

(`numeric_contradiction` above consumes the second).  For `D = ⊥` (`|D| = 1`) both are
automatic.  For `D ≠ ⊥` the non-emptiness `𝒮(Q') ≠ ∅` (equivalently `Z(Q₁) ≠ ⊥`, i.e. `Q₁' < Q₁`)
needs **Thompson's theorem that Frobenius kernels are nilpotent**, whose general form is *not* in
this workspace (only the solvable case, `Work.Frobenius.Fpf.isNilpotent_of_fpf_prime`, which needs
`Group.IsSolvable`).  `Work.Frobenius.Nilpotent.Kernel.isNilpotent_kernel_of_forall_hasNormalPComplement`
reduces the general case to the parked `Work.NPC.thompson_npc`.  Independently,
`Work.FeitSibley.Coherence.exists_nontrivial_linear_irr` (proved, this session) supplies a
nontrivial linear character as soon as `↥Q₁` is nilpotent, and
`CharQ/degree_D_scriptS` supplies the degree-`|D|` member of `𝒮` from it.
-/

